  "name": "clock-skew-signal-loss-future-reading",
  "description": "signal_loss opens on an outage; a reading then arrives dated an hour ahead of the clock: the leaf is unknown, the open excursion is held (no hysteresis, no close), clock_anomaly reports last_reading_at an hour ahead, and next_change_at is the instant it comes within 5 minutes; from there it measures: false at 12:55, so the excursion enters hysteresis, and true again once the timeout has passed after the reading's time, which resumes it",
